    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-26",
      "headline": "AI incident hotline and military crisis MOU announced but not yet operational",
      "detail": "On Sept 26 the White House announced a bilateral communication channel for AI incidents and a US-China Super Intelligence Dialogue on AI risks and benefits, with the next AI dialogue scheduled for November 2026 around the APEC summit in Shenzhen. The system is not yet ready; officials expect weeks to finalize, with unclear benchmarks for what counts as a national security incident and noncommittal sign-on from China. Separately, China's Foreign Ministry said Sept 26 the two militaries agreed to conclude a memorandum of understanding on crisis communication and prevention as soon as possible. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent had first floated the AI notification proposal Sept 21 with Vice Premier He Lifeng.",
      "where": "Washington, D.C.",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/26/china-us-to-open-ai-communication-channel-after-summit-white-house-says",
