        "https://www.cfr.org/articles/the-limits-of-trump-and-xis-photo-op-summit"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-01"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "headline": "Washington summit extends trade truce to Jan 10, 2027 with limited tariff relief and sets next meetings",
      "detail": "Trump hosted Xi for a state visit in Washington Sept 23-25, 2026. Xi arrived at Joint Base Andrews Sept 23 and was greeted on the tarmac by Trump; a White House state dinner was held Sept 24 attended by tech executives including Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, OpenAI leadership, Meta, Google, Microsoft, AMD CEO Lisa Su, Apple CEO Tim Cook and Elon Musk; the leaders toured the National Archives Sept 25 before Xi departed from Joint Base Andrews. They agreed to extend the one-year economic/trade truce from November 2025 by two months to Jan 10, 2027, identified $30 billion of non-sensitive goods in each direction for reduced tariffs, and agreed to meet again at the APEC summit in Shenzhen in November 2026 and the G20 summit in Miami in December 2026. A White House fact sheet also listed a likely pledge for China to import at least 10 million metric tons of US coal in each of 2027 and 2028 — single source, not confirmed by Beijing.",
      "where": "Washington, D.C. and Joint Base Andrews, Maryland",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
